Z||000000||anand||04-21-99||11:13 AM||||Hi there! My 85 V6 had been in a barm for a year. When we tried to start the car after it had been sitting for over a year, it wouldn't run. I have put a new ignition module in it, but still nothing. The electrical system just can't produce sparks for the engine to ignite. Anyone can help??
Z||000001||theogre||04-21-99||11:29 AM||||find the "tach filter" and disconect it. trace the wires from the coil/distributor untill you find a small tin can. that's the filter. your tach won't work, but it will eliminate a common cause of you problem. if that device has shorted out the car can't fire the coil.
Z||000002||anand||04-22-99||10:16 AM||||So..the tach won't work. But I assume that if I replace the filter it will work again?
Z||000003||theogre||04-22-99||10:35 AM||||yes
